<header><p class="st-kicker">county · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">County of Gruyère</h1><p class="st-meta">1073 CE – 1555 CE (approx.) · capital Gruyères</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Swiss Alpine county known for cheese and cattle, whose counts went bankrupt and lost their lands to Fribourg and Bern.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The first known count of Gruyère, Rudolf, appears around 1073 to 1115 in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sarine">Saane</a> valley of the western Swiss <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a>. The counts built their castle above the small town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gruyeres">Gruyères</a> and ruled a territory of pastures and villages on the borderland between French- and German-speaking <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/swiss-confederation">Switzerland</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The county lived from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> and dairying; the hard cheese produced there gave its name to Gruyère cheese. The counts were <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-savoy">Savoy</a> and allied with Bern and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/canton-of-fribourg">Fribourg</a>. The town and castle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gruyeres">Gruyères</a> were among the most picturesque in the region.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Count Michel of Gruyère fell heavily into debt, and in 1554 to 1555 his creditors, the cities of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/canton-of-fribourg">Fribourg</a> and Bern, divided the county between them. Fribourg kept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gruyeres">Gruyères</a> and the lower valley, while Bern took the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sarine">Saane</a> valley (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saanen">Saanen</a>). The castle is now a museum.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="county, 1073 CE – 1555 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r=